BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python I
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:69fa1734e8af4a2f0070505b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this online course you will learn how Python code works and
  given time to practice. Prior coding knowledge is not necessary.\nPython 
 is an open source programming language that is used for creating web appli
 cations\, web content\, mathematics and system scripting. In this online c
 ourse you will learn how python code works and given time to practice. Pri
 or coding knowledge is not necessary for this introductory class. Key take
 aways will include a working knowledge of variables\, loops\, conditional 
 arguments and much more.\nThis class is for beginners but assumes you have
  a basic understanding of computer skills -- basically\, if you can use a 
 word processor or surf the web\, you can learn Python!\nPrior to the class
 \, participants will need to download and install Python and VS Code onto 
 their personal computers (installation guides provided after registration)
 .\nRegistration is limited and specific instructions including information
  about software installation will be provided.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa1734e8af4a2f0070505b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Asian Heritage Month Film: Double Happiness (1994)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T193000
UID:69ebf5082866a5b4884aaff3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Asian Heritage Month and the first installment of ou
 r new monthly Canadian movie series!\nEast clashes with West as a young Ch
 inese woman struggles to appease her father while pursuing her dreams. Sta
 rring Sandra Oh\, in one of her first critically acclaimed performances.\n
 Film will be shown with closed captions.\nLight refreshments will be serve
 d or feel free to bring your own!\nRated PG-13.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Second floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebf5082866a5b4884aaff3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
UID:69a85b71b48451fc3c069f76@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nThe Romance Book Club title fo
 r Saturday June 11 2026 is\nProblematic Summer Romance\nby Ali Hazelwood.
 \nPlease note that this book club is for individuals 18+.\nLimited copies 
 will be available in branch for pick up.\nDrop in\, no registration requir
 ed.\nThis program was previously scheduled for June 6 and has been re-sche
 duled to June 13.
LOCATION:Maryvale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a85b71b48451fc3c069f76
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scrabble Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T153000
UID:69e16419b6c4ac1fedccea6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Put your word skills to the test! Join us for some friendly Sc
 rabble in a relaxed\, welcoming space. Whether you are a triple-word-score
  pro or new to the game\, all adults are welcome.\nDrop-in\, no registrati
 on required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e16419b6c4ac1fedccea6d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T161500
UID:69d576cdc1cf6f9a7583d8be@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The North York Central Library Film Club meets monthly on Wedn
 esdays. There is a short\, informal discussion after the screening\, time 
 permitting. All films begin at 2:00 pm in the Auditorium.\nRegistration is
  not required. Please contact the Browsery Department at 416-395-5672 for 
 more information.\nHamnet (2025)\nRunning time: 125 minutes\nDirector: Chl
 oé Zhao\nStarring: Jessie Buckley\, Paul Mescal\, Emily Watson\, and Joe 
 Alwyn\nWilliam Shakespeare falls for the free-spirited Agnes. Their whirlw
 ind romance leads to marriage and three children\, but as Will's theatrica
 l ambitions draw him to London\, Agnes remains behind to manage the househ
 old. When tragedy strikes\, their bond is deeply tested-but through grief 
 and resilience\, their journey inspires the creation of Shakespeare's time
 less masterpiece\, Hamlet.\nNext dates:\nJune 24 : The Great Escaper
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d576cdc1cf6f9a7583d8be
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
